{
  "uid": "pg-connector-issue-jira",
  "title": "pg-connector-issue-jira",
  "description": "The pg-connector-issue-jira daemon: the Atlassian rate-limit reading against the configured floor, requests by result, queues, freshness, where answers are served from, change detection delay, settle results, consumer lag and redeliveries, tracked and watched sets, and the local store.",
  "tags": ["pg-connector", "pg-connector-issue-jira"],
  "schemaVersion": 39,
  "editable": false,
  "graphTooltip": 0,
  "time": {
    "from": "now-24h",
    "to": "now"
  },
  "refresh": "1m",
  "templating": {
    "list": []
  },
  "panels": [
    {
      "id": 1,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Rate-limit headroom against the floor",
      "description": "The Atlassian burst window as the last response reported it: requests remaining (origin_remaining), the window size (origin_limit), the configured floor (origin_floor, rate_reserve_requests: nothing spends below it) and the headroom (remaining minus floor; negative means the floor is breached). The series are absent while no reading is current, and the line breaks there on purpose: a gap means no reading, not healthy headroom. The alert rule 'pg-connector-issue-jira origin budget is below its floor' fires on the 10-minute average headroom held for 5 minutes, so a brief dip on this panel does not page.",
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 0,
        "w": 24,
        "h": 9
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "max(pg_connector_issue_jira_origin_remaining)",
          "range": true,
          "legendFormat": "remaining"
        },
        {
          "refId": "B",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "max(pg_connector_issue_jira_origin_limit)",
          "range": true,
          "legendFormat": "limit"
        },
        {
          "refId": "C",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "max(pg_connector_issue_jira_origin_floor)",
          "range": true,
          "legendFormat": "floor"
        },
        {
          "refId": "D",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "max(pg_connector_issue_jira_origin_headroom)",
          "range": true,
          "legendFormat": "headroom (remaining minus floor)"
        }
      ],
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom"
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi"
        }
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "color": {
            "mode": "palette-classic"
          },
          "custom": {
            "lineWidth": 1,
            "fillOpacity": 0,
            "spanNulls": false
          }
        },
        "overrides": [
          {
            "matcher": {
              "id": "byName",
              "options": "floor"
            },
            "properties": [
              {
                "id": "color",
                "value": {
                  "mode": "fixed",
                  "fixedColor": "red"
                }
              },
              {
                "id": "custom.lineStyle",
                "value": {
                  "fill": "dash",
                  "dash": [10, 10]
                }
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Jira requests by result",
      "description": "Requests the daemon made to Jira per second, by result (ok, error, rate_limited, unauthenticated or refused), over the dashboard's rate interval. A growing rate_limited or unauthenticated series is the first sign of trouble; refused counts requests the daemon declined to send. The Loki alert rules 'daemon rate limited' and 'daemon authentication failing' (pg-connector-issue-jira) watch the same conditions in the event log.",
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 9,
        "w": 12,
        "h": 8
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "sum by (result) (rate(pg_connector_issue_jira_jira_requests[$__rate_interval]))",
          "range": true,
          "legendFormat": "{{result}}"
        }
      ],
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom"
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi"
        }
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "reqps",
          "color": {
            "mode": "palette-classic"
          },
          "custom": {
            "lineWidth": 1,
            "fillOpacity": 0
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      }
    },
